  "body": {
    "id": "lem:ambient-subset-population-flag-class",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "The bounded calibrated class is a subclass of the population flag class:\n\\[\n \\Theta\\subseteq\\Theta_{\\mathrm{pop}}.\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\Theta",
      "\\Theta_{\\mathrm{pop}}"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:source-independence",
      "ass:all-absolute-moments",
      "ass:calibration-rank",
      "ass:latent-profile-plane",
      "def:ambient-class",
      "def:population-flag-class"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(\\theta\\in\\Theta\\).  The ambient-class definition supplies the same three structural equations as the population-class definition.  Its source-independence member property supplies mutual independence within every environment, its all-absolute-moments member property supplies finite absolute moments of every positive integer order, its calibration-rank property gives \\(\\operatorname{rank}(C)=d\\), and its latent-profile-plane property gives \\(u_k\\in A\\) for every integer \\(k\\geq2\\).  These are precisely the substantive membership requirements of \\(\\Theta_{\\mathrm{pop}}\\), with the positive-dimension and environment-indexing conditions supplying the shared typing conditions.  The remaining centering, coefficient, moment-envelope, order-cap, and singular-gap restrictions defining \\(\\Theta\\) only make the class smaller.  Thus \\(\\theta\\in\\Theta_{\\mathrm{pop}}\\), proving the inclusion.",
    "justification": "This lemma formally separates population identification from the additional bounded inference and legal-swap restrictions.",
    "gap": "The broad and bounded classes must be related explicitly rather than conflated by notation.",
    "consumer": "The bounded cancellation corollary and the population identification theorem use this inclusion.",
